     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily (15 g/day) is a toxic dose, and I know of no clinical indication for it. A single 5000 mg dose is already in the range where acute liver injury is a concern. Three of those in a day could cause severe hepatotoxicity or liver failure in a 70 kg patient, whatever their baseline liver function.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** Examples are 650 mg or 1000 mg PO, with a frequency and daily maximum that fit your patient (typically no more than 3\u20134 g/day).\n- **Add a note to the order**, such as a daily maximum or \"do not exceed 4 g/24h from all sources.\"\n- **Help you think through the clinical goal.** If you're trying to get stronger analgesia or treat fever, I can help you consider adjuncts or alternatives.\n\nIf you think there's a special circumstance I'm missing, please talk to pharmacy or your attending before going further. If you give me the dose you want, I'll enter it."
      }
